/target
# /logs is scratch, except the two the documents cite by line number:
# requirements.md §3 attributes each backend failure to a line of
# c_build.log, and differences/ATTRIBUTION.md's ulp table is read off
# libm_differential.log. Citations nobody can open are not citations.
/logs/*
!/logs/c_build.log
!/logs/libm_differential.log
# summary.txt is the gate result; evidence/purerust-libm-gate/ holds the
# copies the documents cite, so the live one stays scratch.
.claude/

# Runtime artifacts examples write into their CWD (stats CSVs, solution
# trajectories). Root-anchored so real repo data files keep tracking —
# e.g. crates/sundials_core/src/sundials_utils_cvec.txt, the printf
# reference vectors.
/*.csv
/*.txt
